## Repo-specific rules (handwritten)

- **`WRFrontiersDB-Parser`: do development in the `WRFrontiersDB-Parser-dev` worktree,
  never in the main checkout.** `/srv/dev/repos/WRFrontiersDB-Parser` is the checkout
  the WRF pipeline runs (the Orchestrator resolves the Parser at
  `<repos_dir>/WRFrontiersDB-Parser`), so it must stay on `main`, clean, and
  fast-forwardable — an edit or a feature branch there goes straight into the next
  pipeline run. Do all feature/fix work in `/srv/dev/repos/WRFrontiersDB-Parser-dev` (a
  `git worktree` of the same repo): branch off `origin/main` there (`main` itself is held
  by the main checkout), commit, and open PRs from there. Only touch the main checkout to
  fast-forward it after a merge (e.g. `wrf-pull`).
